  "checked": "Henry 2002-03: 24 PL goals, 20 PL assists (record then), PFA Players' Player and FWA (FourFourTwo, Squawka, Wikipedia PL 2002-03). Arsenal 8 points clear on 2 March 2003 (Wikipedia PL 2002-03, premierleague.com season review); Arsenal 2-3 Leeds at Highbury on 4 May 2003 handed United the title (Sports Mole, premierleague.com). Final table top six from Wikipedia's table (W/D/L/GF/GA), United 83 v Arsenal 78. 2003 vote: Nedved 190 (27 first places), Henry 128 (8), Maldini 123 (7) (Wikipedia, RSSSF, UEFA). Juve won 2002-03 Serie A; Nedved booked in the semi against Real Madrid, missed the final; Milan won on penalties after 0-0 at Old Trafford, 28 May 2003 (Wikipedia Juve season, UEFA, Forza Italian Football). 2003-04 unbeaten, Henry 30 league goals; Henry PL goals by season 17, 17, 24, 24, 30, 25 (Wikipedia, FourFourTwo). 2004: Shevchenko 175, Deco 139, Ronaldinho 133, Henry 4th on 80 (Wikipedia, CBC). Football365's 'myth' argument kept for balance. No Henry game footage yet, so no gameclip.",
